---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import now from '../data/now.json';
import skills from '../data/skills.json';
import projects from '../data/projects.json';
import publications from '../data/publications.json';
import patents from '../data/patents.json';
import { getSortedPosts, formatDate } from '../lib/posts';

const latest = (await getSortedPosts()).slice(0, 3);

const layers = [
  { name: 'Web apps', depth: 'L0 · user', href: '/projects/#web', hue: 'yellow' },
  { name: 'Languages · Go, Java, Python', depth: 'L1 · lang', href: '/projects/#compilers', hue: 'orange' },
  { name: 'C', depth: 'L2 · lang', href: '/projects/#systems', hue: 'red' },
  { name: 'Assembly', depth: 'L3 · asm', href: '/blog/bytes-in-memory/', hue: 'brown' },
  { name: 'ISA · RISC-V', depth: 'L4 · isa', href: '/research/#publications', hue: 'violet' },
  { name: 'Microarchitecture', depth: 'L5 · uarch', href: '/research/#publications', hue: 'blue' },
  { name: 'RTL / Verilog', depth: 'L6 · rtl', href: '/projects/#compilers', hue: 'teal' },
  { name: 'Gates', depth: 'L7 · gates', href: '/research/#experience', hue: 'green' },
  { name: 'Transistors', depth: 'L8 · silicon', href: '/research/#experience', hue: 'gray' },
];

let pin = 0;
const pins = skills.flatMap((g) => g.items.map((item) => ({ n: ++pin, group: g.label, item })));
---

<Page nav="home" title={null} description="Aman Pathak - PhD Scholar in computer architecture, hardware security, and low-level systems. RISC-V, side-channel attacks, formal verification." ogImage="/og/home.png">
  <p class="sec-label">VAJRADEVAM-01 · §0 identity</p>
  <h1 style="font-size:1.35rem;max-width:40ch;font-weight:700">Aman Pathak · PhD Scholar, hardware security · RISC-V · low-level software.</h1>

  <Figure no="1" caption="Abstraction stack, top to bottom. Scroll to peel away layers; each label links to the relevant section. Without motion or script, the stack reads as a static figure.">
    <div class="stack-fig stack-peel" id="stackFig" role="list" aria-label="Abstraction stack from web apps down to transistors">
      {layers.map((l, i) => (
        <div class="stack-layer" role="listitem" data-depth={i} id={`layer-${i}`} style={`--band:var(--h-${l.hue})`}>
          <a href={l.href}>{l.name}</a>
          <span class="depth">{l.depth}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Figure>

  <section data-layer="0" aria-label="Top layers">
    <h2 class="sec-head" id="about">§1 · At the top of the stack <a class="anchor" href="#about" aria-label="Link to section">§</a></h2>
    <p>
      I'm a PhD Scholar in the Department of Computer Science and Information Systems at
      BITS Pilani KK Birla Goa Campus, working at the intersection of hardware security,
      RISC-V architectures, and low-level software. My current work spans side-channel
      mitigation, formal verification of cache coherency, and ML-based malware analysis on
      embedded binaries. Earlier, I designed Ku/X-band antennas at KIIT, and I have six
      patents filed in the RISC-V space covering data-flow integrity, crypto engines, and
      on-chip ML.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem">Field notes from the upper layers · <a href="/projects/">{projects.length} projects</a> on record, <a href="/blog/">journal entries</a> on architecture, compilers, and C.</p>
  </section>

  <section data-layer="3" aria-label="Middle layers">
    <h2 class="sec-head" id="middle">§2 · Mid-stack: C, assembly, ISA <a class="anchor" href="#middle" aria-label="Link to section">§</a></h2>
    <p>
      Outside of research, I spend a lot of time building things close to the metal. I've written
      a TCP/IP stack from scratch, a malloc replacement, a cycle-accurate 6502 emulator, a
      container runtime using raw namespaces and seccomp, a bytecode VM in Go, and neural networks
      built purely from matrix operations. This is not an exhaustive list, I keep adding projects
      to my profile as a hobby. I also write about these topics on my blog, where I've published
      posts on architecture, compilers, and C. And I teach sometimes.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem">Probes at this depth ·
      <a href="https://github.com/vajradevam/vajrip">vajrip</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/vajradevam/memoria">memoria</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/vajradevam/whale">whale</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/vajradevam/commodore64">commodore64</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/vajradevam/rv32i-SingleBus-emulator">rv32i-emulator</a>
    </p>

    <h3 class="sec-head" id="now" style="font-size:1.2rem">Now · register file <a class="anchor" href="#now" aria-label="Link to Now">§</a></h3>
    <table class="spec responsive">
      <caption>Table 3 · Currently live registers. Contents change without notice.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {now.map((item, i) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-th="Address" class="addr">0x{(i * 4).toString(16).padStart(4, '0').toUpperCase()}</td>
            <td data-th="Name">now+{i}</td>
            <td data-th="Description">{item}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section data-layer="6" aria-label="Bottom layers">
    <h2 class="sec-head" id="bottom">§3 · Bottom of the stack <a class="anchor" href="#bottom" aria-label="Link to section">§</a></h2>
    <p>
      Low-level stuff intrigues me. A C program is nothing but bytes in memory, there is no
      abstraction beyond that. Sure, memory is made of transistors and semiconductors, and VLSI
      gives us gates and voltages and whatnot, but C, and the assembly it compiles to, is quite
      magical. I know exactly what it is going to do, and nothing is hidden. It is the naked, and
      quite often the bitter, truth. More than low levels <em>per se</em>, to borrow from
      category theory, I am interested in the stripped-down, non-abstracted, naked-truth stuff.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem">At silicon level · <a href="/research/#publications">{publications.length} publications</a>, <a href="/research/#patents">{patents.length} patents filed</a>, <a href="/research/#experience">full record</a>.</p>

    <h3 class="sec-head" id="skills" style="font-size:1.2rem">Skills · pin-out <a class="anchor" href="#skills" aria-label="Link to Skills">§</a></h3>
    <table class="spec responsive">
      <caption>Table 4 · Pin-out, grouped by bank · Languages / Systems / Domains.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Pin</th><th scope="col">Bank</th><th scope="col">Signal</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {pins.map((p) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-th="Pin" class="addr">P-{String(p.n).padStart(2, '0')}</td>
            <td data-th="Bank">{p.group}</td>
            <td data-th="Signal">{p.item}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Latest journal entries">
    <h2 class="sec-head" id="latest">§4 · Latest entries <a class="anchor" href="#latest" aria-label="Link to section">§</a></h2>
    {latest.map((post) => (
      <div class="entry">
        <span class="eno"><time datetime={post.data.pubDate.toISOString()}>{formatDate(post.data.pubDate)}</time></span>
        <div>
          <h3><a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>{post.data.title}</a></h3>
          {post.data.description && <p class="esummary">{post.data.description}</p>}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
    <p style="margin-top:1rem"><a href="/blog/">All entries <Arrow dir="right" /></a></p>
  </section>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/home.ts';
  </script>
</Page>
